For compact cars and sedans, pricing typically depends on factors like distance, availability of space on the trailer, and the level of protection required. Generally, local transportation within a 250-mile radius will have lower rates compared to long-distance journeys, which can span thousands of miles. To ensure optimal space utilization and cost-effectiveness, car carriers might group vehicles of similar size together, offering competitive pricing for compact cars.

